**phase-059 — complete.**

**Reproduced** (at `d514651`): REPL printed 2 lines via `Display`; `rb run` printed 4 for the same program.

**Fixed**: `src/repl/mod.rs` — `execute_code_from` now prints `render_error(&style, code, file, &e)` = `Error::render(code, Some(file))` over the session buffer, run through `paint_diagnostic` (label line + `-->` line + caret line in `Paint::Error`; source line left plain). Two production lines plus three small functions; `Error::render` itself untouched.

**12 new tests** (6 `edge_*`), all asserting on escape-stripped text or against `Style::forced(..)`: source line + caret, byte-identical to `Error::render` with colour off, REPL-vs-`rb run` location diff via the real `run_file_with_diagnostic` path, tree-walker-vs-`BytecodeVm` rendering equality, plus block/multiline-span, no-span, span-past-the-buffer, empty line, 500-char line, unicode, colour-contract cases. One end-to-end test through the `rb` binary.

**Gates**: `cargo fmt --check` pass · `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings` pass · `cargo test --all-targets` 1744 passed / 0 failed (62 binaries) · `cargo test --doc` 2 passed. `./rbops/verify.sh` **not run — `rbops/` is not in this checkout** (`ls rbops/` → no such directory), reported honestly in REPORT.md and FINDINGS.md.

**One DoD mismatch, reported not papered over**: the caret for `say nosuchvar` lands at column 1, not under `nosuchvar`, because the analyzer records the statement's span — `rb run` prints the same caret for the same program. Moving it is a language-wide span change, recorded as F1 in `phases/phase-059/FINDINGS.md` for the auditor. The test asserts column 1 *and* column 13 (`set x to 1 +`) so a renderer pinned to the first column cannot pass.

